---
description: Hono on Bun — route modules, shared Zod, db package only
globs: apps/api/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# API (`apps/api`)

Bun-native server. Do not add Node, `@hono/node-server`, Express, or CORS.

```ts
// ✅ src/index.ts
app.route("/", healthRoutes);
app.route("/", authRoutes);
app.route("/", workspaceRoutes);
app.route("/", projectRoutes);
app.route("/", boardRoutes);
app.route("/", commentRoutes);
app.route("/", eventRoutes);
```

`src/index.ts` also exports `app` for tests (keep the Bun `export default`).

- One Hono app per route file (`new Hono()`), then `app.route("/", …)`.
- Product routes use `new Hono<SessionEnv>()` and `requireSession`
  (`src/middleware/session.ts`): `auth.api.getSession`, no session → 401
  `{ error }`, else `c.get("userId")`. Authorization order: session →
  membership (query in `@agentic-kanban/db`; missing or not a member → 404,
  never 403) → `workspace_id` from the DB row, never from body/query/params →
  every tenant query filters by it. Params use `@hono/zod-validator`.
- Build every response (including 401/404 `{ error }`) and pass it through
  `.parse()` of the shared schema before `c.json`; dates go out as ISO strings.
- Validate inputs (param/json via `zValidator` → 400) and responses with
  `@agentic-kanban/schemas`.
- `src/routes/board.ts` (`boardRoutes`): `GET /api/projects/:projectId/board`,
  `POST /api/projects/:projectId/tasks`, `PATCH`/`DELETE /api/tasks/:taskId`,
  `POST /api/tasks/:taskId/move` (`moveTaskBodySchema` → 200 task; the target
  column is validated against the task's own project, else 404).
  Data comes from the `*ForMember` queries in `@agentic-kanban/db`. Client ids
  only identify: `columnId` is validated against the authorized project (else
  404, no IDOR). `DELETE` answers 204 (`c.body(null, 204)`). Each write
  publishes one event through the local `announce(event)` helper (wraps
  `publish` in try/catch + `console.error`: the write is already committed, so
  a publish failure never changes the HTTP response). It is called right after
  the `*ForMember` query returns a row (transaction committed) and before
  answering; 404 and 400 publish nothing. `projectId` comes from the row,
  `actorUserId` from the session (`c.get("userId")`), never from the body.
  `task.created`/`task.updated` carry the same `toTaskResponse` body that is
  returned; `task.deleted` carries `taskId`; `task.moved` carries the final
  `columnId`/`position` of the reread row.
- `src/routes/comments.ts` (`commentRoutes`): `GET`/`POST /api/tasks/:taskId/comments`
  (`createCommentBodySchema` → 201 `commentSchema`; list by `created_at` ASC with
  `authorName` from `user.name`). Authorization comes from the task row:
  `listCommentsForMember`/`createCommentForMember` join the task with
  `workspace_member`; no task or not a member → 404 and `workspace_id`/`project_id`
  are copied from that row. No mentions, email or SSE publishing yet.
- Database access only through `@agentic-kanban/db`. Never import
  `@libsql/client` or `drizzle-orm` from the API.
- Better Auth (`src/auth/index.ts`, email/password, cookie session) is served
  by `src/routes/auth.ts` on `/api/auth/*` via `auth.handler(c.req.raw)`. Do
  not wrap those routes with `@hono/zod-validator`; Better Auth validates.
- `authRateLimit` (`src/auth/rate-limit.ts`): in-memory, 10/min per route on
  `POST` sign-up/sign-in, then 429. Off with `NODE_ENV=test` or
  `AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED=1`. `get-session` is never limited.
- Realtime stays in this process. No Socket.IO, Redis, or extra service.
  `src/realtime/index.ts` is the in-memory hub: `subscribe(projectId,
  listener)` returns the unsubscribe function (empty sets are deleted) and
  `publish(event)` parses with `boardEventSchema` and delivers only to that
  `projectId`; a throwing listener is logged and does not stop the others.
  `listenerCount(projectId)` exists for tests.
- `src/routes/events.ts` (`eventRoutes`): `GET /api/projects/:projectId/events`
  (`requireSession` → `getProjectForMember`, else 404) answers with
  `streamSSE`. Only the `streamSSE` callback loop writes to the stream: hub
  listeners and the keepalive timer just enqueue/flag and wake the loop
  (writing from another request's context did not reach the client in Bun).
  Frames carry only `data: JSON` (no `event:`); comments `: connected` on open
  and `: keepalive` every 15 s. Headers `Cache-Control: no-cache, no-transform`
  (set after `streamSSE`, which overwrites it) and `X-Accel-Buffering: no`.
  `onAbort` unsubscribes and clears the timer.
- Bun idles out requests after 10 s: `src/index.ts` sets `idleTimeout: 0` and
  `fetch(request, server)` calls `server.timeout(request, 0)` for paths ending
  in `/events` (never pass `server` to `app.fetch`, its 2nd arg is `env`).
  The stream checks session and membership only when it opens. The
  Vite+ `/api` proxy uses `timeout: 0` and `proxyTimeout: 0` (no `ws`).
- Do not auto-run migrations or seed (apply with `docker compose exec api bun run db:migrate`, then `bun run db:seed`). Dev: `bun run --hot`. Listen
  `0.0.0.0:${API_PORT:-3000}`.
